{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>If the Levite come.</b> One might think the verse speaks of an unconditional Levite — therefore Scripture says <b>and minister</b>: this excludes Levites who are not fit for service (Sifrei)." "<b>And come with all the desire of his soul, and minister.</b> This teaches about a priest who comes and offers his freewill or obligatory offerings even in a watch that is not his (Bava Kama 109); another interpretation — it further teaches about priests who come for the festival that they offer (in the watch) and perform the service for the offerings that come on account of the festival, such as the festival musafim, even though the watch is not theirs (Sifrei; Sukkah 55)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:33.923434667Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}